course: dictionary
lesson: 4600
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the sentence and ask which meaning fits. «Hero» is a good example, because the dictionary gives it three meanings.
explain: The first meaning is a person who does something very brave or good, especially to help or save others. «Heroes come in every size: a village woman planting a tree in Kenya, a nine-year-old boy in Germany starting a tree campaign, or you counting birds in your garden for scientists.» Here, hero means someone who helps.
explain: The second meaning is the main character in a story, film or play. «In the story, the hero faces danger and solves the problem.» Here, hero means the character the story follows, and the opposite is the villain.
explain: The third meaning is someone you admire very much. If you say «My hero is my grandad», you mean he is the person you look up to most. Always check: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: A hero is a person who does something very brave or good, especially to help or save others.
fact: Hero can also mean the main character in a story, film or play.
fact: Your hero is someone you admire very much.
fact: The plural of hero is heroes, because -o words like potato and tomato add -es.
fact: A superhero is a hero with special powers, as in comics and films.
exercise: «Heroes come in every size: a village woman planting a tree in Kenya.» What does hero mean in this sentence? | A tall, strong person | *Someone who does something brave or good to help others | The main character in a film | A person who writes stories
exercise: «In the story, the hero faces danger and solves the problem.» What is the hero in this sentence? | The villain | A place where the story happens | The person who wrote the story | *The main character
exercise: Which is the correct plural of hero? | heros | *heroes | heroies
test: Which sentence uses hero to mean the main character? | My hero is my swimming coach | *The hero of the book finds a secret map | The nurse was a hero at the hospital | The lifeguard jumped in to save the boy
test: Lifeguards and firefighters who save people are called heroes. What does hero mean here? | A person who draws murals | Someone with special powers only | The main character in a play | *A person who does something brave to help others
exam: Mia says, «My hero is my grandad, who taught me to swim.» Which meaning of hero is used? | The main character of a story | A person who does something brave to save others | A superhero with special powers | *Someone you admire very much
